issue(id="0018" status="open")
  title Extend HTML import root selection beyond tag paths
  user-story
    as-a maintainer of the puggers HTML converter
    i-want root selection to support useful non-tag selectors
    so-that users can target meaningful regions without depending only on tag structure
  premise.
    Task `0013` introduces explicit `root` / `--root` selection with a small
    tag-only path grammar. That keeps the first structural extraction pass easy
    to explain and test, but real HTML often identifies meaningful regions with
    `id`, `class`, ARIA roles, data attributes, or other attributes. This task
    should extend the root-selection grammar deliberately rather than slipping
    toward an accidental partial CSS selector engine.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Decide which non-tag selector forms belong in puggers root paths first, such as `#id`, `.class`, `[attr]`, or `[attr=value]`, and document the boundary.
    criterion Add focused tests that cover matching, first-match ordering, no-match behavior, and interactions with direct-child `>` and descendant whitespace.
    criterion Keep unsupported selector syntax rejected with clear parse errors instead of silently falling back to tag matching.
    criterion Update CLI and core documentation with shell-safe examples for any selector syntax that needs quoting.
    criterion Keep the design compatible with future CLI, library, and npm surfaces without requiring a full CSS selector API.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Confirm whether the first selector expansion should prioritize `#id` / `.class` or attribute selectors.
    item(status="open") Decide whether selector matching should use source attributes even when those attributes are not retained in rendered Pug.
